---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/content/Section.astro';
import Table from '../components/content/Table.astro';
import StatusPill from '../components/content/StatusPill.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/content/Placeholder.astro';
import Note from '../components/content/Note.astro';
import { judging, statusLabels } from '../data/judging';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';

const toc = [
  { id: 'where-to-look', title: 'Where to look' },
  { id: 'five-minutes', title: 'If you only have five minutes' },
  { id: 'contribution', title: 'Contribution' },
  { id: 'how-we-mark-evidence', title: 'How we mark evidence' },
];

const pillKind = { ready: 'met', partial: 'open', missing: 'unmet' } as const;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Judging guide"
  lede="A map from each iGEM criterion to the page that holds the evidence, with an honest status for each one."
  toc={toc}
>
  <Section id="where-to-look" title="Where to look">
    <p>
      This table is our own mapping, not iGEM's. It exists so that an evaluator does not have to guess where something
      lives, and so that we cannot quietly leave a gap unmarked.
    </p>

    <Table label="iGEM criteria and where the evidence is">
      <table class="data">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Criterion</th>
            <th scope="col">What it covers</th>
            <th scope="col">Where</th>
            <th scope="col">Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            judging.map((item) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{item.criterion}</th>
                <td>{item.what}</td>
                <td>
                  <a href={href(item.where)}>{item.whereLabel}</a>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <StatusPill kind={pillKind[item.status]} label={statusLabels[item.status]} />
                  {item.note && <p class="status-note">{item.note}</p>}
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </Table>

    <Placeholder title="Check against the current iGEM handbook" where="src/data/judging.ts" compact>
      Medal criteria and required pages change between years. Confirm this list against the iGEM 2026 judging handbook
      and add any criterion we have missed.
    </Placeholder>
  </Section>

  <Section id="five-minutes" title="If you only have five minutes">
    <ol class="quick">
      <li>
        <a href={href('problem')}>The problem</a>, with the numbers behind it: lung cancer burden worldwide and in
        Kazakhstan, and why CT screening is hard to reach.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('/')}>The simulation on the home page</a>: one breath through the array, including a confounder
        example that shows why a pattern is not a diagnosis.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('synthetic-biology')}>The biology</a>: what a sensing module is, and which parts of it are still
        undecided.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('experiments')}>The experimental plan</a>: four hypotheses, each with the result that would prove
        it wrong.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('results')}>Results</a>: empty, deliberately, and marked as such.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('safety-and-security')}>Limitations and safety</a>: what would make this fail, and what would be
        required before clinical use.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <Section id="contribution" title="Contribution">
    <p>
      What we want to leave behind for other teams: a documented design for a cross-reactive biological sensing array,
      an analysis pipeline written down before the data exists, and this wiki as an open template for presenting a
      project honestly, including its gaps.
    </p>
    <Placeholder title="Contribution record" where="src/data/judging.ts">
      <ul>
        <li>Parts contributed to the registry, with characterisation data.</li>
        <li>Protocols, analysis code and datasets published for reuse.</li>
        <li>Anything another team could pick up directly, and where to find it.</li>
      </ul>
    </Placeholder>
  </Section>

  <Section id="how-we-mark-evidence" title="How we mark evidence">
    <p>
      The same markers appear on every page, so that the difference between a cited fact, our expectation and a gap is
      visible at a glance.
    </p>
    <dl class="markers">
      <div>
        <dt>A superscript number</dt>
        <dd>A claim supported by a published source. The number links to the full reference and means the same source on every page.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Hypothesis to test</dt>
        <dd>Something we expect but have not shown. Written so that it can be proven wrong.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Limitation</dt>
        <dd>A known weakness, confounder or open problem.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Content or data needed</dt>
        <dd>A gap. It names what is missing and which file it belongs in, rather than being filled with something plausible.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Illustrative</dt>
        <dd>A schematic or simulation used to explain an idea. Never measured data.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <Note kind="context" title="Why an empty Results page">
      <p>
        A figure that looks like evidence and is not is worse than no figure. The chart components on{' '}
        <a href={href('results')}>Results</a> are built and tested, and they render real data the moment it is added.
      </p>
    </Note>
  </Section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .status-note {
    margin-top: var(--sp-2);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 30ch;
  }

  .quick {
    margin: var(--sp-6) 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: quick;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .quick li {
    counter-increment: quick;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.25rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    padding-block: var(--sp-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .quick li::before {
    content: counter(quick);
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .markers {
    margin: var(--sp-6) 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .markers div {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
    padding-block: var(--sp-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .markers div {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 8fr);
      gap: var(--sp-5);
    }
  }

  .markers dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .markers dd {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
</style>
